 * The corpus is hand-crafted so that:
 *   • several documents are clearly on-topic (expect high similarity)
 *   • a couple of documents are tangentially related (expect mid-band similarity)
 *   • several documents are clearly off-topic (expect low similarity)
 *
 * This spread is what makes the threshold effect visible: a low threshold
 * pulls in the tangentially-related docs, a high threshold filters them out
 * and keeps only the highly on-topic ones.
 */
interface CorpusItem {
  /** Free-form semantic label — useful for debugging, not sent to the API. */
  label: "on_topic" | "tangential" | "off_topic";
